<title>USA: Clinton wishes U.S. trade deficit with Japan lower.</title>
<headline>Clinton wishes U.S. trade deficit with Japan lower.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton said Thursday he wished the U.S. trade deficit with Japan was not so high and said he would discuss the matter with Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto.</p>
<p>Asked before a meeting with Hashimoto whether he would raise the issue of the trade imbalance, Clinton said: &quot;Well, I wish they weren't so high but we're going to discus that.&quot;</p>
</text>
